{
  "file": "./02_Knowledge/technologies/services/forgejo/backup-restore.md",
  "folder": "02_Knowledge",
  "types": {
    "source": [
      {
        "severity": "S1",
        "issue": "First cited source is a placeholder on the reserved invalid TLD `example.invalid`; it cannot resolve and is not a live or authoritative URL. The same dead URL is repeated verbatim in the Sources section.",
        "evidence": "frontmatter line 8: url: \"https://example.invalid/forgejo/restore\" (title \"Forgejo restore guide\"); repeated at line 43: \"Forgejo restore guide: https://example.invalid/forgejo/restore\". Fetch of https://example.invalid/forgejo/restore returns a transport error.",
        "fix_hint": "Replace with a live, authoritative source (e.g. the Forgejo backup/restore doc) or remove the placeholder entry and its Sources line entirely."
      },
      {
        "severity": "S1",
        "issue": "Second cited source URL is dead (HTTP 404). The Forgejo backup-and-restore page does exist, but not at the cited path, so the note's evidence as written no longer resolves.",
        "evidence": "frontmatter line 10: url: \"https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/backup-and-restore/\" — GET returns 404. The live page is https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/setup/backup/ (linked from https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/).",
        "fix_hint": "Correct the URL to https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/setup/backup/ (and the sibling's identical citation)."
      }
    ],
    "accuracy": [
      {
        "severity": "S2",
        "issue": "The prose states the HTTP listener runs on port 3000, but the accompanying app.ini example sets HTTP_PORT = 3001. The config contradicts the note's own text (and the sibling's port 3000), which will send a reader restoring the instance to the wrong port.",
        "evidence": "line 31-32: \"Forgejo's HTTP listener runs on port 3000, so a restore must not change the configured port.\" followed by lines 34-37: [server] / HTTP_PORT = 3001.",
        "fix_hint": "Make the config block agree with the stated port (HTTP_PORT = 3000), or correct the prose if 3001 is the homelab's actual configured port."
      }
    ],
    "scope": [
      {
        "severity": "S3",
        "issue": "Contains a `## History` section recounting Forgejo's fork from Gitea in 2022 and the lineage of its backup tooling — technology history/origin story, which the root conventions explicitly exclude from notes.",
        "evidence": "lines 23-26: \"## History\" / \"Forgejo was forked from Gitea in 2022, and its backup tooling inherited that lineage. The restore command has been stable since the fork.\" Root AGENTS.md: \"Do not include technology history, origin stories, or sales/marketing points.\"",
        "fix_hint": "Delete the `## History` section; keep only restore-relevant, homelab-applicable content."
      }
    ],
    "structure": [
      {
        "severity": "S4",
        "issue": "Required frontmatter field `last_audit_date` is missing. It is part of the mandatory 02_Knowledge frontmatter block.",
        "evidence": "frontmatter lines 1-14 contain title, status, author, date, tags, sources, related_docs — no last_audit_date. 02_Knowledge/AGENTS.md frontmatter spec includes `last_audit_date: YYYY-MM-DD` and \"Set `last_audit_date` on every edit\".",
        "fix_hint": "Add `last_audit_date: 2026-10-21` (ISO 8601) to the frontmatter."
      },
      {
        "severity": "S4",
        "issue": "Tags are not lowercase kebab-case: `Forgejo` has uppercase letters and `Restore_Procedure` has uppercase letters and an underscore, violating the tag pattern.",
        "evidence": "line 6: tags: [Forgejo, Restore_Procedure]. Required pattern: ^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$ (root AGENTS.md).",
        "fix_hint": "Rewrite as e.g. tags: [forgejo, restore-procedure]."
      },
      {
        "severity": "S4",
        "issue": "The ini config block is not labeled as \"Example — abstract\" or \"Example — real config\" as required by the section conventions.",
        "evidence": "lines 34-37 show a bare ```ini block with no preceding label. 02_Knowledge/AGENTS.md: \"Both abstract examples and real configs are welcome — label each block as 'Example — abstract' or 'Example — real config'\".",
        "fix_hint": "Add an \"Example — abstract\" (or \"Example — real config\") label above the code block."
      }
    ],
    "overlap": [
      {
        "severity": "S4",
        "issue": "Duplicates claims already made in the sibling note instead of linking to it: the restore procedure and the HTTP port statement are repeated nearly verbatim. The sibling is already referenced via related_docs, so the content should be linked, not restated.",
        "evidence": "target line 30 \"Stop the instance, restore the dump, then start it again.\" ≈ sibling line 22-23 \"Stop the instance, restore the dump, then start it again -- the same steps a restore follows.\"; target line 31 \"Forgejo's HTTP listener runs on port 3000\" ≈ sibling line 24 \"Forgejo's HTTP listener runs on port 3000.\"",
        "fix_hint": "Remove the restated claims and cross-link to ./02_Knowledge/technologies/services/forgejo/dump-schedule.md via related_docs instead."
      }
    ]
  },
  "totals": { "S1": 2, "S2": 1, "S3": 1, "S4": 4 },
  "verdict": "issues"
}
